{"title":"Career Roadmap · Government Teacher","role":"Government Teacher","summary":"A Government Teacher works in government or government-supported schools to teach students according to the prescribed curriculum, assess learning, provide academic support and contribute to the overall development of learners.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Ed (Bachelor of Education)","Course":"B.Ed - Subject Pedagogy (Science / Maths / Social Studies / Languages / Commerce)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Government Teacher works in government or government-supported schools to teach students according to the prescribed curriculum, assess learning, provide academic support and contribute to the overall development of learners."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the recruitment level, subject qualification and state rules, government teaching opportunities may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Primary teacher"},{"text":"Upper-primary teacher"},{"text":"Secondary-school teacher"},{"text":"Subject teacher"},{"text":"Language teacher"},{"text":"Science teacher"},{"text":"Mathematics teacher"},{"text":"Social Studies teacher"},{"text":"Commerce teacher"},{"text":"Special-category teaching roles where separately qualified"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Recruitment commonly involves some combination of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Required academic qualification"},{"text":"Teacher-training qualification"},{"text":"TET eligibility where applicable"},{"text":"State-specific recruitment examination/process such as DSC or equivalent"},{"text":"Merit/rank"},{"text":"Document verification"},{"text":"Reservation/category requirements where applicable"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"Government-teacher eligibility is not identical across India. It depends on the teaching level, subject, state recruitment rules and the specific notification. TET qualification al