oard use"},{"text":"Classroom management"},{"text":"Parent communication"},{"text":"Co-curricular activities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Teaching workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Curriculum","Learning Objectives","Lesson Plan","Teaching Activity","Student Interaction","Assessment","Feedback","Remedial / Enrichment Support"]}]},{"heading":"Subject Pedagogy","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The candidate should develop two complementary competencies:"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Subject mastery"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mathematics","Algebra","Geometry","Calculus / Higher Concepts","School-Level Curriculum"]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Teaching mastery"},{"type":"flow","items":["Concept","Student Difficulty","Teaching Strategy","Activity","Assessment","Feedback"]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong government-teacher candidate therefore needs both what to teach and how to teach it."}]},{"heading":"Core Technical Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill Area","Key Competency"],"rows":[[{"text":"Subject Knowledge"},{"text":"Strong command of teaching subject"}],[{"text":"Pedagogy"},{"text":"Subject-specific teaching methods"}],[{"text":"Lesson Planning"},{"text":"Structured lesson design"}],[{"text":"Classroom Management"},{"text":"Maintaining productive learning environment"}],[{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Tests, rubrics and formative assessment"}],[{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Clear verbal/written communication"}],[{"text":"Inclusive Education"},{"text":"Supporting diverse learners"}],[{"text":"Educational Technology"},{"text":"Digital teaching tools"}],[{"text":"Remedial Teaching"},{"text":"Supporting struggling students"}],[{"text":"Differentiated Instruction"},{"text":"Adapting instruction"}],[{"text":"Data Literacy"},{"text":"Student performance analysis"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Academic records"}],[{"text":"Professional Ethics"},{"text":"Responsible teaching"}]]}]},{"heading":"Lesson P